sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant TD as TeardownCommand
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant IB as EC2 Image Builder

    Note over User,IB: baas admin deployment teardown -- needs the elevated BaasCliDeployerPolicy.<br/>Nothing survives it: empties the bucket, deletes the CORE stack (bucket and results table with it),<br/>then retires the runner image `admin image build` created outside it. The CI stack is untouched.
    User->>TD: baas admin deployment teardown [--deployment] [--yes]
    Note over TD: ConfigService.load() from ~/.baas/config.yaml<br/>stack = the configured prefix (the stack IS the prefix) -- a different --deployment was refused already

    rect rgb(255, 235, 235)
        Note over TD,EC2: Gate 1 -- never tear down under a live job
        TD->>EC2: describeInstances(tag baas-role=benchmark-runner, state=pending|running)
        EC2-->>TD: instances, with each one's baas-job-id tag
        alt running runner instances found
            TD-->>User: abort naming each job id (from the tag), instance and state,<br/>and `baas jobs terminate <jobId>` -- exit 1. No table read: the deployer has none
        end
    end

    TD-->>User: warn: the stack, the bucket and the results table, every job and<br/>measurement in them, and the image will be deleted -- none of it recoverable
    opt --yes not set
        Note over TD,User: Gate 2 -- explicit confirmation
        alt no terminal to ask on
            TD-->>User: refuse, pass --yes -- exit 1, nothing deleted (U32)
        end
        TD->>User: prompt: type the deployment name to confirm deletion
        User-->>TD: typed input
        alt input does not match the deployment name exactly
            TD-->>User: "Aborted. Nothing was deleted." exit 1
        end
    end

    TD->>CF: describeStacks -> RunnerImageExtensionData
    CF-->>TD: the deployed extension, or empty
    opt an extension is deployed
        Note over TD: written with its marker to runner-image-extension.<prefix>.yaml<br/>beside the config file -- the stack holds its only copy (U40).<br/>Cannot read or write it -> exit 1, nothing deleted
    end

    Note over TD,S3: CloudFormation will not delete a non-empty bucket, so it is emptied first
    TD->>S3: list every object version and delete marker, delete them in batches
    alt emptying fails
        TD-->>User: error naming the bucket -- exit 1, the stack is NOT deleted
    end

    TD->>CF: deleteStack(stackName)
    CF-->>TD: delete accepted
    TD->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackDeleteComplete()
    loop poll DescribeStacks
        CF-->>TD: status = DELETE_IN_PROGRESS
    end
    CF-->>TD: status = DELETE_COMPLETE -- the bucket and the results table are gone with it

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
        Note over TD,IB: Retire the runner image -- always, AFTER the stack (a failed stack deletion keeps an image to run on).<br/>prefix = the deployment torn down (--deployment), not this machine's. No step fails the teardown.
        TD->>SSM: getParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id)
        opt pointer present and its AMI still exists
            TD->>EC2: describeImages -- collect snapshot ids
            TD->>EC2: deregisterImage(ami), deleteSnapshot(each)
        end
        TD->>SSM: deleteParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id) -- even if the AMI could not be retired
        TD->>IB: listImages(owner Self, name <prefix>-recipe-runner) + listImageBuildVersions
        TD->>IB: deleteImage(each build version)
        alt everything removed
            TD-->>User: "Runner image retired ... needs baas admin image build before baas run"
        else something failed
            TD-->>User: warn: each leftover, with the aws command that removes it (exit stays 0)
        end
    end

    TD-->>User: exit 0 -- nothing of the deployment is left in the account
